#
# THE REGISTRY TOTAL IS ARITHMETIC, not a reading. It is the sum of every
# budget in the table above, each of which is a worst-of-three, so the total is
# a sum of worst cases and no single run should be expected to hit it.
#
# The figure is no longer repeated in this sentence, and that is the fix rather
# than an omission. It read 356.4 over 27 budgets while the table said 357.4
# over 28, because central updated the table on 2026-10-13 and left the
# sentence describing it. That is the same hardcoded-count failure this block
# warns about four paragraphs down, committed inside the warning. Read the
# total off the table.
#
# Three full passes at the 27-budget size on 2026-10-13 read 308.8 s warm, then
# 365.2 s and 352.1 s cold, so the arithmetic sat inside the cold spread. The warm number is 47 s short of it, and 38 of
# those 47 are the drill gate, which gives up that much of its 54.4 when
# .drill-gate-state is already there. The other 9 s are spread across the
# registry and not attributed. `scripts/test --list` is the authority on what
# runs, and this block is the authority on nothing.
#
# Assertion counts are gone from this table on purpose. This script does not
# aggregate one, so every total written here was a hand-count that went stale
# — and the SUITE count in the sibling rules file was three out of date twice
# for the same reason. `bash scripts/test --list` is the authority.
#
# If a row here ever disagrees with a suite's own final line, the suite is
# right and this comment is stale.
#
# THE TIER GAP HAS INVERTED, AND THE DRIFT NUDGE'S 3.0x RESTED ON IT.
#
# The boundary itself has not moved and is not a wall clock: a suite that runs
# TLC's MODEL CHECKER belongs in slow, and the paragraph below says why the
# JVM is the wrong test. What HAS moved is the gap either side of it. This
# header used to read "the cut is at the 4.2x gap between 2.4 s and 10.2 s",
# then "the 1.5x gap between 4.8 s and 7.4 s", and on 2026-10-13 bead
# tla-ocpw took it past zero: the reading corpus gate was SLOW at 4.1 s, which
# was cheaper than spike measurement, the most expensive FAST row at 4.8 s.
#
# THE INVERSION HAS SINCE CLOSED, and saying so is the point rather than an
# erratum. That gate was 4.1 s over 6 items and is 12.9 s over 25, so it is
# now dearer than every fast row and the two numbers no longer cross. Bead
# tla-8q8n re-based it on 2026-10-14.
#
# The argument the inversion illustrated does not rest on it. Spike
# measurement runs three real TLC jobs against 3-by-3 fixtures and stays fast
# deliberately. The reading gate model-checks every item of a growing corpus
# and is slow for that reason and no other. A tier split on the model checker
# is free to invert on a wall clock whether or not it currently does, so
# nobody should read the tier column as a cost ordering.
#
# That finishes off a stated justification further down this header: "A 3x
# threshold therefore catches every possible tier crossing by construction."
# At a 1.5x gap it no longer did. With the tiers overlapping there is no gap
# left to argue from at all. BUDGET_DRIFT_FACTOR is left at 3 here, because
# re-deciding it needs a human — tla-kqry's own note asks whether the nudge's
# AND is right at all, observing that it never fires on a slow suite that
# merely doubles and never on a fast suite that grows tenfold from 0.5 s, so
# the two halves protect different sizes and nothing protects the middle.
# Recorded here as a measured fact rather than acted on.
#
# WHAT MOVED SINCE THE ROWS WERE LAST TAKEN, and which moves are attributed.
#
#   ATTRIBUTED, cause named in tla-kqry or in git:
#     grader            59.1 -> 99.0 s   tla-8kgj added 26 fixture files;
#                                        tla-kqry measured 90.4 mid-wave
#     seeded bugs       46.9 -> 57.8 s   tla-r2ih's liveness pair, measured
#                                        at 48.1 then 50.8 on the way here
#     spike measurement  1.9 ->  4.8 s   tla-83lg's nine comment-shape
#                                        fixtures
#     spike measurement  4.8 ->  7.5 s   tla-ng7r's two channel fixtures,
#                                        two more real TLC runs
#     drill corpus gate 10.3 -> 54.4 s   32 items landed against a budget
