  # THE COMPLETION CORPUS GATE, added by bead tla-4yit. It is both the
  # instrument's controls and the full sweep of the real tree, because part 3
  # runs harness/completion-gate.sh over completion/ in both tiers. A separate
  # row wired at the gate would re-run the same 48.3 s of TLC, and the bead's
  # brief asked for one; it was collapsed into this row deliberately and that
  # deviation is reported on the bead rather than left to be noticed here.
  #
  # SLOW by the rule in this header rather than by its wall clock, and it is
  # the most TLC-heavy row per item in the registry. Checks 1 and 2 measure a
  # hole by filling it with `TRUE` and re-running every machine, so a two-hole
  # item costs four signatures over three machines — the reference, one per
  # hole, and all-TRUE — which is twelve TLC runs. Four of part 1's fixtures
  # and one of part 2's are real checking items for the same reason, so they
  # cost twelve each as well.
  #
  # ITS COST TRACKS THE ITEM COUNT AND THE HOLE COUNT, not this file. Measured
  # 2026-10-14 on the 9-item tree, standalone over three back-to-back serial
  # runs: 73.518 / 73.786 / 77.970 s, so 78.0 is the slowest rounded up.
