  # 48.044 / 48.223 / 48.296, which is about 5.4 s per item, and the fixtures
  # are the other 25 s. So 18 items is about 127 s and 36 items about 224 s. A
  # fixed second count is the wrong KIND of budget for a corpus whose purpose
  # is to grow: when this row drifts, divide by the item count first. An item
  # with three holes costs a third more than one with two, so divide by the
  # hole count too.
  #
  # THE CHEAP LEVER IF IT GETS TIGHT is the reference run, and it should be
  # declined. It is one signature of the four and it is what makes the other
  # three measurements of a delta from a number somebody checked. Dropping it
  # would leave check 1 comparing against EXPECT alone, and an ANSWER.md that
  # does not score EXPECT would then be invisible. The honest lever is the
  # fixture count in part 1, never the corpus.
